--TEST--
`Core\Server::traceId` throws a `LogicError` in a program that answers no request, while `isDraining` in the same class still answers — `rule:security/request-state-throws-in-an-isolate`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The runtime draws a trace for every run, so the member could return one here.
// It throws instead: the id belongs to a request, and a command-line program
// has none. `isDraining` is a fact about the process and keeps answering.
try {
    echo Core\Server::traceId(), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "LogicError\n";
}
if (Core\Server::isDraining()) {
    echo "draining\n";
} else {
    echo "accepting\n";
}
--EXPECT--
LogicError
accepting
